  BottomSheet: {"title":"Overlay/Bottom Sheet","category":"Overlay","displayName":"Bottom Sheet","description":"A mobile touch sheet that rises from the bottom edge, with animated entrance and exit, a grab handle, optional drag-to-resize snap points, and purpose-controlled dismissal. Like Dialog, it is a padded container: content starts at the theme's bottom-sheet padding (--spacing-4 by default), and a lone Section child or bleed children such as Table and Divider align against it. A sheet always owns a native <dialog>; inside the deprecated BottomSheetSwitcher the switcher presents and closes that dialog as the flow moves between steps. In both modes, ref and shared DOM props target the visual panel <div>. Sheets stack: a sheet opened while another is open sits on top of it, the covered sheet stays mounted and recedes, and one scrim covers the page. A sheet that closes as another opens in the same update is replaced by it, with the step-to-step handoff a multi-step flow needs.","hidden":false,"component":"BottomSheet/BottomSheet.astro","demo":"BottomSheet/BottomSheet.demo.astro","subComponents":{}},
  BottomSheetSwitcher: {"title":"Overlay/Bottom Sheet Switcher","category":"Overlay","displayName":"Bottom Sheet Switcher","description":"Deprecated: write each step as its own BottomSheet with isOpen, controlled by one state value that names the open step. Closing the top sheet and opening the next in the same update, from a control inside the open step, runs the same replace handoff (see BottomSheet, Replacing a sheet), with no sheetId and no switcher; a step changed from a control outside the flow (a page control, or code after focus left the step) closes and opens with ordinary push and pop motion. BottomSheetSwitcher keeps working until a future minor release removes it: a flow used on its own behaves as released (with two fixes: a toast raised from a step renders above the flow and can be pressed, and under reduced motion its steps follow the reduced-motion rule), and a flow stacked with other sheets is one level of the stack (it recedes and is blocked when covered, shares the one scrim, and stands down from dismissal while covered). Modal and hasScrim={false} flows migrate the same way. Coordinates multiple BottomSheets as a mutually exclusive flow. One activeSheet ID selects the only interactive sheet; during a handoff, the new sheet enters above the inert previous sheet. If the new sheet is shorter, the previous sheet simultaneously moves down until their top edges align, then fades after both transforms complete. Each child sheet renders its own native <dialog>: a modal flow presents each sheet with showModal(), as a standalone modal sheet does, so the browser supplies modality (the page is inert and focus stays in the top-layer dialog, so both hold across a handoff) and the switcher holds the shared body scroll lock once for the whole modal flow. A no-scrim flow presents each sheet with show() inside the isolated flow wrapper of the switcher, which orders the step dialogs with local values; this differs from a standalone hasScrim={false} sheet, which is hosted in the top layer as a manual popover with no page-level z-index, and it is one reason to migrate. The switcher coordinates the rest: one scrim paints at a time, focus returns to the element that opened the flow, its ref, id, and data-testid resolve to the dialog hosting the active sheet, and its other dialog props and handlers apply to every sheet dialog.","hidden":false,"component":"BottomSheet/BottomSheetSwitcher.astro","demo":"BottomSheet/BottomSheetSwitcher.demo.astro","subComponents":{}},
