  InternationalizationProvider: {"title":"Utility/Internationalization Provider","category":"Utility","displayName":"Internationalization Provider","description":"Wraps your app to set the active locale and (optionally) merge additional translation catalogs + per-locale overrides. Astryx components inside the subtree resolve their strings against this context. If no provider is present, components fall back to the shipped English defaults.","hidden":true,"component":"i18n/InternationalizationProvider.astro","demo":"i18n/InternationalizationProvider.demo.astro","subComponents":{}},
  Item: {"title":"Table & List/Item","category":"Table & List","displayName":"Item","description":"A single, flexible item primitive that unifies the \"start content + label + description + end content\" pattern across Astryx. Use it wherever you need a structured row: dropdown menus, selectors, contact lists, notifications, file browsers, and activity feeds.","hidden":true,"component":"Item/Item.astro","demo":"Item/Item.demo.astro","subComponents":{}},
  Kbd: {"title":"Content/Kbd","category":"Content","displayName":"Kbd","description":"Renders a keyboard shortcut as styled key badges. Use Kbd in tooltips, menus, and help text to show key combinations.","hidden":false,"component":"Kbd/Kbd.astro","demo":"Kbd/Kbd.demo.astro","subComponents":{}},
  Layer: {"title":"Utility/Layer","category":"Utility","displayName":"Layer","description":"Layer utilities provide the app-level provider used by overlay systems. Use LayerProvider at the app root for toast/layer configuration; use higher-level Popover, HoverCard, or Tooltip APIs for most overlay UI. Rendered layer content, not the provider’s application subtree, uses theme body text defaults and exits ancestor surface/group membership. Establish intentional groups and complete required providers inside each layer. Every anchored layer keeps a gutter from each viewport edge — the spacing-4 step or the device safe-area inset, whichever is larger — and is capped to the viewport, never to the room beside its trigger: an explicit width renders at its size, flips when it does not fit beside the trigger, and slides into view when it fits on neither side. An app that floats a persistent bar over a viewport edge declares it once as inset on LayerProvider (blockStart, blockEnd, inlineStart, inlineEnd); each edge adds to that edge’s gutter for every anchored layer and moves the toast viewport by the same amount, and defaults to zero. The inset is app configuration, not a theme value.","hidden":false,"component":"Layer/Layer.astro","demo":"Layer/Layer.demo.astro","subComponents":{}},
